  "question": {
    "text": "The maximum area of rectangle inscribed in a circle of diameter $R$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$R^2$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{R^2}{2}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{R^2}{4}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{R^2}{8}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "According to question,\n<img src=\"assets\\st0001_c67b6acb511f.png\"/>\nDiameter $=R$\nDiagonals, $d_1=d_2=R$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n\\text { Max Area of rectangle (any quadrilateral) } & =\\frac{1}{2} d_1 \\times d_2 \\\\\n= & \\frac{1}{2} \\times R \\times R=\\frac{R^2}{2}\n\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}